// How the script lowering runs each special (`SPECIAL_*`) (`extract::codegen::Support`, Milestone 8).
// Generated once in Wave 0 from the decomp names; classified by Task J. Decomp names only.
//
// - Native: `prelude::special` runs it (every Native has an arm there, checked by
//   `tests/m8_j_specials.rs`). Specials whose Gen3 screen does not exist yet answer as
//   cancelled, report `Degraded` and fade the field back in when the script faded it out.
// - Ignore: no effect on the engine's state; nothing is emitted.
// - Default(v): `v` is written where the special writes its result (`specialvar`'s var, else
//   VAR_RESULT), with no report.
// - Unsupported: `Report::Unsupported("SPECIAL_*")`, logged; the script continues.
// Every Native, Ignore and Default, and every special reachable on the Act 1 maps (checked by
// `tests/m8_j_specials.rs` against the decomp), gives a reason.
// The 483 specials named by a `special`/`specialvar` line of the decomp (`data/**/*.inc` and
// `data/*.s`, `data/specials.inc` excluded) are classified; the other 41 are Unsupported.
//
// Counts: 64 Native, 19 Ignore, 83 Default, 358 Unsupported.
{
    "SPECIAL_AccessHallOfFamePC": Unsupported, // post-game; unreachable: ScriptMenu_CreatePCMultichoice answers B
    "SPECIAL_Bag_ChooseBerry": Native, // degraded: no bag screen, nothing chosen; fades back in
